WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.300
<v Manager>Good afternoon everyone. Let's start, we have one hour and three topics.</v>

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.400
<v Manager>First the Q3 incidents, then the four-eyes check proposal, and at the end tooling, if we have time.</v>

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.300
<v Manager>Twenty minutes per topic. Team Lead, can you start with the incidents?</v>

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:13.400
<v Team Lead>Sure. In Q3 we had two duplicate payments. The biggest one: Peeters IT Solutions, invoice INV-2026-0412, seven thousand eight hundred euros, paid twice in August.</v>

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.300
<v Team Lead>The invoice came in by e-mail and by post, and two different people processed it.</v>

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.000
<v Manager>Ok, ok.</v>

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.400
<v Employee B>That was me and A, actually. We only noticed when the contractor called.</v>

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.300
<v Employee A>Yeah. They were honest about it, at least.</v>

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.200
<v Team Lead>We recovered the money in September, but it took three weeks.</v>

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.000
<v Manager>Noted.</v>

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:17.400
<v Team Lead>The second one was smaller, a few hundred euros, same pattern.</v>

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.300
<v Manager>So the root cause is the same twice.</v>

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:11.400
<v Team Lead>What I would like everyone to do from now on: before paying a contractor invoice, search the payment log by the invoice number and the contractor's VAT number.</v>

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:16.300
<v Team Lead>If either one is already there, stop and check before paying.</v>

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.400
<v Manager>Ok, ok. That's simple enough.</v>

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.300
<v Manager>Second topic. Team Lead, your proposal for the four-eyes check.</v>

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:11.400
<v Team Lead>Yes. I propose a four-eyes check for every contractor invoice above five thousand euros.</v>

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.300
<v Employee B>Why not every invoice above two and a half thousand?</v>

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:20.400
<v Team Lead>That would double the checks, we don't have the people for that.</v>

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:25.300
<v Employee B>But the risk is the same, a duplicate is a duplicate.</v>

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:32.400
<v Employee A>I think five thousand is fine, honestly. Most small invoices are recurring anyway.</v>

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:42.400
<v Manager>Ok, ok. So, decision: every contractor invoice above five thousand euros gets a four-eyes check, starting with the November run.</v>

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.300
<v Team Lead>Agreed, I'll make sure the team applies it.</v>

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:47.800
<v Employee B>Ok.</v>

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:07.400
<v Employee A>Speaking of contractors — as in our DmfA entry, freelancers are declared quarterly, so for Q4 we should also—</v>

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:15.400
<v Senior Expert>Sorry, I have to correct that: freelancers are not declared in the DmfA, that's the employer declaration for employees.</v>

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:20.400
<v Senior Expert>Self-employed people pay their contributions through their social insurance fund.</v>

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:24.300
<v Employee A>Well, I'm quite sure I read it somewhere...</v>

00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:30.400
<v Senior Expert>I understand the confusion, but the DmfA is only for employees. I can send you the reference.</v>

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:34.300
<v Employee A>Hm. You're right, I mixed that up in the entry.</v>

00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:37.400
<v Manager>Then please update that entry.</v>

00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:39.000
<v Employee A>Will do.</v>

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:04.300
<v Manager>Last topic, tooling. I don't think we have enough time today.</v>

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:08.300
<v Manager>Tooling we'll discuss next quarter.</v>

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:10.200
<v Team Lead>Fine by me.</v>

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:33.400
<v Manager>Thank you all. Good session.</v>
